    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2QV2MYLrWDakEzdRwv4jThx)_\n\nReplaces #22, which GitHub would not reopen after its branch was rebased (#18 to #20 are merged into `main`, so this PR is no longer stacked).\n\n**Before:** about thirty modules spelled out `~/notes`, `~/bibliography`, `~/Documents/literature`, `~/src` and the like, so the configuration only worked with one machine's layout and a test run could not be kept away from the real notes. `init.el` ended in a Custom block with a list of `/Users/siainbuletin/notes/...` agenda files, which made `org-agenda` open every one of them. The system modules sat in their own `env/` directory.\n\n**After:**\n- A new first module, `sp-paths`, names each location once (`sp-notes-dir`, `sp-documents-dir`, `sp-literature-dir`, `sp-bibliography-dir`, `sp-org-dir`, `sp-src-dir`, `sp-git-dir`, `sp-clones-dir`, `sp-data-home`, `sp-yadm-repo`, `sp-chrome-history-file`) and offers `sp-path` to build a path below one. The modules use these instead of literals. Each location can be overridden from the environment (`SP_NOTES_DIR`, `SP_BIBLIOGRAPHY_DIR`, `SP_DOCUMENTS_DIR`, `SP_ORG_DIR`, `SP_SRC_DIR`, `SP_GIT_DIR`, `SP_CLONES_DIR`, `XDG_DATA_HOME`). Defaults come from `~`, and the Chrome history path has a macOS, Windows and Linux default.\n- `env/` moves to `base/` (`sp-env`, `sp-exwm`, `sp-macos`, `sp-syslinux`, `sp-syswin`), in `libraries/modules/` and in `docs/tangles/`. The tangle paths, `docs/main.org` and `conditional-loading.org` follow. `sp-env` requires `sp-paths` and explains in its commentary that the `SP_*` overrides are read before the shell environment is imported.\n- The whole Custom block at the end of `init.el` is removed, so `sp-vulpea-para` decides which agenda files load.\n\n**Behaviour notes:**\n- On your Mac every path default resolves to what it was before.\n- Removing the Custom block also drops what it set besides the agenda files (fonts, `sia/modeline`, `custom-safe-themes`, `package-selected-packages`, `helm-minibuffer-history-key`, `transient-show-menu`, `bibtex-aux-opt-alist` and the four `org-extra-emphasis` faces). They fall back to defaults until set in a module.\n\n**How:** the literate sources in `docs/tangles/` are edited together with the modules. The branch content is the same as #22 (rebased onto `main` with the merged #20); I did not start the full configuration, so please try a launch on your Mac.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01C6awF5FLwSCZyLWz41VV6Y)_",
